config AUDIO_CODEC_ES8311
	bool "Everest Semiconductor ES8311 audio codec"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_EVEREST_ES8311_ENABLED
	select I2C
	help
	  Enable the ES8311 mono ADC/DAC with I2C control and standard I2S:
	  two 16-bit slots, MSB first, normal clock polarity. The codec must
	  receive continuous bit and frame clocks from the I2S controller.

	  Set audio_codec_cfg.mclk_freq to the external MCLK frequency at
	  256 times the sample rate. Supported rates are 8000, 11025, 12000,
	  16000, 22050, 24000, 32000, 44100 and 48000 Hz. Zero selects BCLK
	  multiplication, limited to 32000, 44100 and 48000 Hz by the 1 MHz
	  multiplier-input minimum for 3.3 V operation.

	  Input and output volume use whole dB, clamped to -95 through +32 dB.
	  Capture uses differential MIC1, a DT-selected PGA gain and a fixed
	  +24 dB digital scale before input volume. Output uses headphone mode.

	  Configuration leaves both directions muted. Start the I2S transport
	  before audio_codec_start(); a stopped direction applies its cached
	  volume and mute on start. Use audio_codec_apply_properties() for
	  running directions. A failed property unmute stops each direction
	  rolled back to mute; call audio_codec_start() to retry.

	  Check audio_codec_stop() before stopping I2S clocks. The application
	  manages regulators, clocks and external amplifiers; device PM is not
	  implemented. Supplies must be available before initialization, or use
	  zephyr,deferred-init and device_init() after enabling them. Muting
	  cannot be guaranteed when I2C fails; validate analog settling and
	  power transitions on the board.
